{"timestamp": 1778129240.1915555, "duration_sec": 1.9005162715911865, "validator_hotkey": "5FZe9Mpo5dLXfhGZ4VjRnw6dmz9LVPp6nzqPyDfaS9BLKs33", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "testnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "Yeah. Yeah, man."], [1, "Well, Hickson, there's a video of him, and he did this multiple times where he would go to these gyms and he would teach a seminar, like a long seminar, and then roll with all the black belts and just tap them one after the other. One\u2014 world champions, guys that just didn't understand what was going on. Like, how is this happening? Oh yeah, like Paulo Filho when he was a WEC world champion and he was\u2014 he had won the Mundials, I believe. He'd won multiple jiu-jitsu championships. And he trained with Hickson. He's like, man, it's true. He goes, I can't believe it. He goes, that guy treated me like I didn't even belong in there. It was crazy. And Hickson by that time was probably like 40."], [0, "Yeah."], [1, "You know, and he's still just dominating guys on the mat and effortless. It wasn't strength. It was, it was just pure technique and movement."], [0, "Basics and just mastering of basics. Oh yeah."], [1, "Basics. It was like, there's none of the, no berimbolos and no X guard, nothing crazy. Everything he did is like, like jiu-jitsu 101, but to a masterful, masterful degree."], [0, "Yeah. It was incredible. And telling people that, you know, 'cause everybody knows Royce, and I'm like, you guys don't know who his big brother is."], [1, "Is Royce. He would openly say that my brother's 10 times better than me."], [0, "Right, yeah. Yeah. Yeah, so, you know, that really put, and I love jiu-jitsu because it's held up the tradition. That martial arts, so much of karate lost because it became a business. And people would just, you know, put their time in and pay for their black belts. And it just watered it down. And all these people running around saying that they're master this and, you know, grand whatever and all these made-up things. And it's like, oh yeah, the guy's a master in an Asian martial art. That's a\u2014 English word, right? You know what I mean? How did master sneak its way into it? Yeah, but anyway, but you know, male ego, you know."], [1, "Well, the thing about martial arts other than jiu-jitsu is when you're sparring, it's very controlled. Like a lot of karate sparring is very controlled. A lot of taekwondo sparring is very controlled. But in jiu-jitsu, the beautiful thing about grappling is you know how good everybody is because they all spar. They're all rolling with each other and they essentially go on full blast until the tap."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Comedy"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["brazilian jiu jitsu", "grappling", "martial arts", "technique", "fundamentals", "training", "sparring", "seminars", "competition", "black belts", "self defense", "karate", "taekwondo", "tradition"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
