{"timestamp": 1778130812.9798126, "duration_sec": 5.838597774505615, "validator_hotkey": "5DkzbwTnocecNohGP4aNVcHZfUgx8uA1MGQ4WB1u3kfi78gE", "task_type": "named_entities_extraction", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "named_entities_extraction", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "document", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "Community Planning and\nHousing\nMinutes\nTuesday, April 28, 2026, 1:30 PM\nChair: Sarah Parady, Vice Chair: Diana Romero Campbell\nMembers: Flor Alvidrez, Shontel Lewis, Amanda Sandoval, Amanda Sawyer, Jamie Torres\nStaff: Luke Palmisano\nAttendance\nPresent 7 - Alvidrez, Lewis, Romero Campbell, Sandoval, Torres, Parady, Watson\nAbsent 1 - Sawyer\nAction Items\n26-0557 Approves a map amendment to rezone property from B-8, Waivers, UO-1,\nUO-2 to S-MX-8, located at 8401 East Belleview Avenue, in Council\nDistrict 4.\nA motion offered by Vice Chair Romero Campbell, duly seconded by Council\nmember Alvidrez, that Council Bill 26-0557 be approved for filing, carried by the\nfollowing vote:\nAye: 6 - Alvidrez, Lewis, Romero Campbell, Sandoval, Torres, Parady\nNay: 0\nAbsent: 1 - Sawyer\n26-0561 Amends Chapter 27, Article III, Section 27-45 through 27-52 of the Denver\nRevised Municipal Code (\u201cDRMC\u201d). Article III, referred to as the\nPreservation of Affordable Housing Ordinance.\nA motion offered by Council membe"], [0, "Page 3 - Denver, CO Zoning Code Sample\nShopfront C-MS-5 C-MS-8 C-MS-12 Height C-MX-3 C-MX-5 C-MX-8 C-MX-12 C-MX-16 C-MX-20 Stories (max) 3 5 8 12 16 20 A Feet (min/max) na/45\u2019 24\u2019/70\u2019 24\u2019/110\u2019 24\u2019/150\u2019 24\u2019/200\u2019 24\u2019/250\u2019 Height Exceptions See Section 7.3.7.1 C-MS-5 C-MS-8 C-MS-12 Siting C-MX-3 C-MX-5 C-MX-8 C-MX-12 C-MX-16 C-MX-20 Required BUILD-TO 75% 0\u2019/5\u2019 B Primary Street (min build-to % within min/max range) Residential Only Buildings: 0\u2019/10\u2019 25% 0\u2019/5\u2019 Side Street (min build-to % within min/max range) C Residential Only Buildings: 0\u2019/10\u2019 Build-to Exceptions and Alternatives See Sections 7.3."], [1, "Department of Housing Stability - City and County of Denver\nApr 16, 2026 \u00b7 The Department of Housing Stability builds a healthy, housed, and connected Denver . We invest resources, create policy, and partner with organizations to keep people in the homes they already live in, to quickly resolve an experience of homelessness, and to connect people to affordable housing opportunities."], [2, "Plans and Reports - City and County of Denver - OpenCities\nLearn more about the Department of Housing Stability\u2019s COVID-19 efforts from Chief Housing Officer Britta Fisher, along with HOST staff and partners from Denver \u2019s Department of Public Health & Environment, presenting an update on COVID-19 operations to City Council\u2019s Safety, Housing , Education, and Homelessness Committee."]], "participants": null}}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "ner_001", "crc": 1321322, "title": "Extract named entities from documents", "name": "extract_named_entities", "description": "Identifies and extracts named entities from provided documents.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "ner", "prompt_template": "Extract all named entities from the provided document. Include the following entity types: PERSON, ORGANIZATION, LOCATION, and any other relevant entities. Return as comma-delimited list of entities with their types (e.g., 'John Smith (PERSON), ACM Corp (ORGANIZATION)). Only return the entities without any additional commentary.", "output_variable": "extracted_entities", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["city and county of denver", "denver", "denver city council", "safety housing education and homelessness committee", "department of housing stability", "department of public health & environment", "opencities", "covid-19 operations", "denver revised municipal code", "denver zoning code", "preservation of affordable housing ordinance", "council bill 26-0557", "action item 26-0557", "council bill 26-0561", "action item 26-0561", "8401 east belleview avenue", "sarah parady", "diana romero campbell", "britta fisher", "shontel lewis"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778131019.035957, "duration_sec": 1.6793787479400635, "validator_hotkey": "5GQyFzvtVMw9X45t6dvUFgR9unFpDCccPPCiAoqJrtPuC8my", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "Yes, correct. Correct. This is just like, we are just scratching the surface by conversations. The analytics piece is where you can tell how did the customer progress? What do they want next? Is there a renewal risk? Is there an upsell opportunity? Those types of things come in with each conversation based on how the customer progressed through the journey. So we have built everything. Are you also plugging in the usage, like the telemetry usage?"], [0, "Yeah, we have to integrate with the CRM to get the usage. And we are not doing that yet because we are a startup. We are an early stage startup. So we want pilot customers to come on board and say, we want you to integrate with Salesforce or Pipedrive or whatever the case may be. And we will absolutely do that. We have the ability to do that. And obviously it's on our roadmap, but we want a customer to come and say, we want this conclusively for us to be able to build it."], [0, "Yeah. Yeah. That makes sense. HubSpot, Monday, whatever, you know. Yeah. Whatever they need. But that is, like you said, you're getting a much better picture because you are"], [0, "taking the customer success feedback and triaging it with not just like, oh, I had a problem here, but more here's what I'm using or here's what I'm doing. And can we see if there are certain types of use cases that are using the product more? Can we see? It's like surfacing all of these unknowns and you get to ask a few questions about your users."], [0, "that maybe it would be a lot harder to figure out or you would need to hire a data analyst or a data scientist to really dig into the data. If you really think about it,"], [0, "Every year, people hire BCG or other management consultants for $300 or $600 an hour to do a project just for this. You don't need to do this anymore. You can record everything. You can give them, not just make your customer success managers like superstars and frankly, not just CSMs, but sales engineers, sales, anybody really superstars because they get real-time answers."], [0, "But on top of it, there's two things that are missed really, which is some CSMs or some sales engineers are better than the others. I mean, that's just the reality, right? And that tribal knowledge is missing. It's in their head."], [0, "So when you capture all this, you can make everyone, you can democratize that knowledge. You can make everyone superstars. So can you imagine if you had like 10 superstars instead of three, how well that would pan out? Like 10 superstars instead of three, how well that would pan out for your organization? You can handle more customers with just those 10 superstars."], [0, "Right? So that's number one. You're democratizing knowledge. You're building knowledge bases. You don't even have to write your own knowledge base. Now you're building knowledge base already with your conversation. Right? You're building knowledge base. You're building analytics. You're building high-level approaches to what to even position to your customers next year. The opportunity is limitless. I'm so bullish on this product because it's"], [0, "The opportunity is really limitless on this. And especially if you can consider, I've seen it. And especially if you tie in sales to customer success, to support, to professional services. Can you imagine like the information flow that goes end to end? Like you can become a beast."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Technology"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title":