n declaring incidents and automatically notifying the right teams. And you can get unified incident response by seamlessly orchestrating alerts and incident triage with on-call scheduling across Slack, Teams, Zoom, desktop, and mobile."], [0, "So what you'll want to do is head on over to lightstep.com forward slash syntax and you'll get a free 30-day trial. Listeners of Syntax will also receive a free LightStep incident response t-shirt after firing an alert or incident. So check it out. Are you in need of incident response? Check out lightstep.com forward slash syntax."], [0, "I do want to ask, you said maybe down the road, like you guys obviously are early days in this type of stuff. You said maybe down the road, might be have a Svelte or maybe Vue. I'm curious about like authoring a library like this. Like how much of the code when you wrote this thing is just JavaScript functions and how much of it is specifically React stuff? Do you have any concept of that? Yeah, we've done..."], [0, "we've had discussions about this too. And I know we've been asked like, okay, how can we strip this down and, and package it in a way that is, um, uh, potentially like agnostic to react just vanilla JavaScript. Um, yeah, I think it's not as much as we would have hoped like, uh, like the, to return to the selected options example where you're selecting a red or blue shoes, um,"], [0, "That is like, it's pretty closely tied to React state management and it's a bunch of React hooks. And so you can't like necessarily strip that out. You can maybe get a couple of utility functions out of it, you know? Yeah. But at what point is that going to be actually beneficial to people? Yeah. It's yet to be seen like how much can be shared and how much of it is just bespoke per framework. Yeah."], [0, "Josh, was it you on, somebody on Twitter, I was asking when the Dino, Node, Cloudflare, Vercel, and Shopify rolled out the JavaScript interop committee. Are you familiar with that one? Yeah, WinterCG. WinterCG, yeah. So I was like, at the time, I was like, I don't know, I get it. I get why Cloudflare would want to be a part of this committee because they want."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Coding"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["javascript", "react", "server components", "web development", "frontend frameworks", "npm packages", "widgets", "state management", "hooks", "framework agnostic", "devops", "sre", "incident response", "on call scheduling", "service monitoring"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
