{"timestamp": 1778141220.3868914, "duration_sec": 5.254489898681641, "validator_hotkey": "5DkzbwTnocecNohGP4aNVcHZfUgx8uA1MGQ4WB1u3kfi78gE", "task_type": "named_entities_extraction", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "named_entities_extraction", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "document", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "September 24, 2025\nA regular meeting of the City Council of the City of Boston was held in the Christopher A. Iannella\nChamber, City Hall on Wednesday, September 24, 2025, at 12:03 P.M.\nPresident Louijeune in the Chair. Present Councilors Breadon, Coletta Zapata, Durkan, FitzGerald,\nFlynn, Mejia, Murphy, Pep\u00e9n, Santana, and Weber. Absent Councilor Worrell.\nReverend Father Alexandros Pretorian of St. Nectarios Greek Orthodox Church, delivered the\ninvocation, and the meeting was opened with the pledge of allegiance.\nThe Chair moved to adopt the minutes from the September 17, 2025 City Council Meeting.\nMotion prevailed.\n_________________________________________________________________________\n1690 Message and order for your approval an Order authorizing the City of\nBoston to appropriate the amount of Two Million Five Hundred Thousand\nDollars ($2,500,000.00) for the purpose of paying the cost of a feasibility\nstudy and schematic design associated with a project for the Ruth Batson\nAcademy,"], [0, "City Council Committee On Public Safety And ... - Boston.gov\nApr 29, 2025 \u00b7 Discussion Topics Docket #0322 Order for a hearing to discuss ways to ensure operations of the 911 system and contingency plans in case of a 911 system outage. This matter was sponsored by Councilor Edward Flynn and Erin Murphy, and was referred to the Committee on January 29, 2025 ."], [1, "Council's public-safety committee holds hearing on 911 ...\nSep 24, 2025 \u00b7 The Council's Committee on Public Safety and 