aking advantage of people when they need something to believe in, and you're asking for all their money. Like, I remember I was watching this guy on TV once, like, televangelists are the worst, and this guy was saying that if you are broke, you should borrow money to donate it to the church, and it will be paid back to you tenfold. That God will pay you back tenfold. And then he had all these examples of people that did it, and they would call in and say, I, I was $1,000 in debt and this and that, but I borrowed $100 and I donated it to you, and now all of a sudden I drive a Rolls-Royce. And it's all horseshit."], [0, "But those are all desperate, desperate people."], [1, "That's for people."], [0, "Those are the same people that, yeah, I'm gonna spend $30 on the lottery every day for like fucking 50 years and don't know how much. That's another scam."], [1, "Yeah, that's another scam. Not only is that a scam, here's the scam about the lottery. Not only does\u2014 like, say if everyone pumps money into the lottery, say you, you buy $100 worth of tickets and Jamie buys $100 worth of tickets and I buy $100, so there's $300 in the lottery. There's not even $300 available to win. Right. So, and then if you win, you don't get all the money. You get the money over a long period of time."], [0, "But they always give you options."], [1, "Right, right, right. But if you, if you take the second option, I mean, it's a significantly\u2014 like, here's a good example of it. Speaking of the Epstein Files, what do you mean speaking of company Zorro Trust?"], [0, "I didn't like that transition. You looked me right in my eyes and said, speaking of the Epstein Files."], [1, "Well, Epstein, we were talking about it before the podcast. No, Epstein came to see you."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Comedy"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "d