rtise and a wide variety of expertly delivered stress test options: The Top Down Model"], [2, "Real Estate Stress Testing: How to Evaluate Your Portfolio\u2019s ...\nJul 30, 2025 \u00b7 Today\u2019s real estate managers don\u2019t need to rely solely on spreadsheets and intuition. Several real estate portfolio management platforms offer built-in stress testing tools or can integrate with financial modeling software: Yardi and MRI provide debt and income tracking features that allow for scenario modeling."]], "participants": []}}, "prompt_chain": null, "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["real estate", "banking", "finance", "risk management", "investment strategy", "financial modeling", "portfolio management", "stress testing", "asset allocation", "portfolio optimization", "machine learning", "data analytics", "commercial real estate", "credit risk", "regulatory compliance", "scenario analysis", "capital adequacy", "algorithmic trading", "property management", "market trends"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778147238.8312924, "duration_sec": 1.7657079696655273, "validator_hotkey": "5FZe9Mpo5dLXfhGZ4VjRnw6dmz9LVPp6nzqPyDfaS9BLKs33", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "testnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "Drinkag1.Com/Rogan."], [1, "Salt is an essential mineral. You need salt to survive. Salt is not the problem. They associate salt with high blood pressure, salt with this, salt with\u2014 it's not true."], [0, "It's bullshit. What type of salt? Is it a different salt?"], [1, "Is it like\u2014 no, it's not. Salt's not bad for you. Well, first of all, there's iodized salt, which is actually good for you because it contains iodine. They add iodine to it, which is good for you. But salt is not a bad thing. I mean, you shouldn't have too much salt. Look, if you eat enough salt, you could die."], [0, "Joe, you can't be the president and educate me with this. So all of these years, it's a\u2014 it's a\u2014 these people getting their toes chopped off Amputated?"], [1, "That's not why. If you're getting diabetes, it's usually from sugar. Okay. You know, there's been a lot of misinformation that's spread because of actual scientists that were bribed by the sugar industry. So the sugar industry, they paid a bunch of Harvard scientists. It was Harvard, right? I believe it was. They didn't even give them a lot of money. Was it the 1950s or 1960s, Jamie? Do you remember? So this has all been outed now, but what they did was they tried to associate saturated fat and, and foods with saturated fat with being responsible for heart disease. And they did that to try to get the blame off of sugar, because sugar is fucking terrible for you. It's terrible in basically every way, especially added sugar."], [0, "So why are all of these diseases that we speak of are more, more happening in the black community than in the white community?"], [1, "It's diet. It's diet. It's 100%."], [0, "It's processed food."], [1, "It's processed food. It's diet. It's sugar. It's sugary drinks. It's the amount of sugar. Like, if you say, if you drink like a 1-liter Pepsi, the amount of sugar that is\u2014 okay, let's find out how much sugar is in a 1-liter Pepsi. If you drink several of these a day, one of them, I believe, is more sugar than you're ever supposed to have in a day."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Comedy"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["nutrition", "salt", "sodium", "blood pressure", "iodine", "sugar", "diabetes", "heart disease", "saturated fat", "processed food", "soft drinks", "diet", "public health", "scientific research", "food industry"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778147525.3442407, "duration_sec": 2.9167094230651855, "validator_hotkey": "5FZe9Mpo5dLXfhGZ4VjRnw6dmz9LVPp6nzqPyDfaS9BLKs33", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "testnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "And at that time you were already training with Maurice Smith."], [1, "Yes, Maurice was one of the guests."], [0, "Right, you were training. Yeah. Because I ended up training with Maurice Smith, you know, every time I'd go to Seattle. You know, we'd train together. So, you know, we're like, part of this like kind of karate martial art nerd culture."], [1, "Yeah."], [0, "When it wasn't even popular."], [1, "No."], [0, "I used to see you all the time. You know, you and, you know, doing jiu-jitsu, Carl Parisian and all these guys at Legends. Where was another place? It was, we had, there was Legends and there was another place."], [1, "The Bomb Squad."], [0, "Yes."], [1, "The Bomb Squad was the first place that Eddie taught at and then that place closed down, then we went to Legends. Yeah. And then we moved to the other Legends that was like in more East LA. Mm-hmm. And then And then Eddie started opening up his own place in downtown."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Comedy"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["martial arts", "karate", "jiu jitsu", "training", "sparring", "gym culture", "combat sports", "fighting", "coaches", "instructors", "seattle", "los angeles", "martial art history", "community", "fitness"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778148058.2750757, "duration_sec": 1.9608745574951172, "validator_hotkey": "5FZe9Mpo5dLXfhGZ4VjRnw6dmz9LVPp6nzqPyDfaS9BLKs33", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "testnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[2, "This was my first party. Look at American people, how they doing just in the street, you know? I don't have places to do it."], [1, "Medina flips through the book fondly, as if he's cooing at baby photos."], [2, "And that's the way Algodones start, you know, with that. And like this, you can see all my book is full of parties, you know, to where I go and everything, you know. Well, it's all my life in this book, you know."], [1, "It's clear that Medina put his heart into these parties, into making the town grow the way it did. He convinced his neighbors to cook enough food to feed thousands for free. He hired a mariachi band and converted an old boxing dressing ring into a stage. And the Americans had a great time. Medina made sure the margaritas were strong."], [2, "And they was drunk like crazy, you know. The American customs told me, Dr. Medina, why you give to those guys?"], [0, "Why?"], [2, "They cross right here, they don't want to show the papers, they tell us son of a bitch and go."], [3, "They was very drunk."], [1, "Year after year, Los Salgadones would continue to throw parties like that first one. Americans would return home, talk of the tacos, the town, their teeth. What was once a town of about 750 when Maga\u00f1a first arrived is now crammed with clinics, hotels, restaurants, and pharmacies. Today, young dentists and souvenir vendors from all over Mexico continue to migrate to town in hopes of finding stable work. And the tourists keep coming in droves."], [2, "In winter, it's too much people and they make lines, and that's uncomfortable for them, but they don't care. They make the lines, you know, and they still coming because they find dental services good, a good price and everything, and very handsome doctors. We live from the tourists, you know."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Society & Culture"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["tourism", "dental care", "mexico", "border town", "parties", "local culture", "food", "mariachi", "hospitality", "american tourists", "immigration", "small business", "economic development", "community events", "travel"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778148271.0849123, "duration_sec": 1.8894610404968262, "validator_hotkey": "5C8LULGoFybR7ybg4S8qQkaaowGXFFja4KmMoSqwhxuAsn33", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "testnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "Good morning, it's February 18th and this is your daily brief in AI. Here's everything you need to know."], [1, "AI takes center stage at BioAsia 2026 in Hyderabad as Asia's leading life sciences and health tech forum opens its 23rd edition with a sharp focus on AI, automation, and data science to accelerate healthcare innovation. More than 175 exhibitors spanning pharmaceuticals, biotechnology, medtech, digital health, and advanced manufacturing showcase a broad tech-bio ecosystem. The event brings researchers, entrepreneurs, investors, and policymakers together to push the tech-bio revolution and address global health challenges. Telangana highlights its strong policies, skilled workforce, and premier educational institutions as key drivers of growth in life sciences. The opening ceremony, led by the State Chief Minister, included the Genome Valley Excellence Award for Cancer Gene Therapy to Professor Bruce L. Levine. Inauguration and awards underscore Telangana's leadership in life sciences and recognize Levine's work in cancer gene therapy. Telangana also unveiled initiatives such as the Young India Skills University and the Telangana School of Life Sciences to build talent in mRNA technology, gene therapy, and AI. Recent moves cited include the Telangana Next Gen Life Sciences Policy, Genome Valley expansion, the launch of OneBio and multiple global capability centers in Hyderabad, The event emphasized ongoing collaborations among research institutions, corporates, startups, MSMEs, and government to create a trusted, future-ready life sciences ecosystem in Telangana. Telangana Rising 2047 envisions making the state a $1 trillion economy by year 2034 and $3 trillion by year 2047 through cross-sector collaboration across research labs, industry, startups, MSMEs, and government. The Telangana Life Sciences Policy 2026-30 promotes cross-border collaboration, international capital, and translation of breakthroughs into healthcare solutions to position Telangana as a global life sciences hub. Plans include shifting from supply-led manufacturing to solution-driven leadership by building talent in mRNA, gene editing, and AI-driven drug discovery, while boosting Hyderabad's role in medical tourism."], [2, "Unilever is partnering with a major cloud provider to run an AI-first digital overhaul, migrating its data and cloud platform to Google Cloud to speed demand generation and deliver actionable insights. The initiative centers on flagship brands Dove, Vaseline, and Hellmann's as consumer journeys become more AI-driven and conversational, aiming to redefine how consumer packaged goods are discovered and shopped. Leaders describe it as a milestone in modernizing legacy systems and boosting agility and consumer engagement in the CPG sector. Market reaction showed UL trading near its 52-week high, with a pre-market around $74.65 and approaching the annual high of $74.97. Unilever reported strong fiscal 2025 results, with total sales up 3.8% to \u20ac50.5 billion across Beauty Wellbeing, personal care, and home care. The collaboration is framed as part of a broader shift toward agentic consumer journeys where AI surfaces influence product discovery and selection. It aims to redefine how brands are found and purchased, aligning with increasingly conversational journeys guided by intelligent digital agents. There is mention of repurposing a former Unilever soap factory in Wales into a modular data center site, signaling broader data infrastructure development alongside the cloud migration. The initiative seeks more personalized consumer engagement and more efficient marketing investments, signaling a move toward AI-driven experiences in the CPG space. Unilever's longstanding relationship with Accenture, renewed in 2024 to scale GenAI, complements Horizon 3 Labs' efforts in Toronto that reportedly runs hundreds of AI applications. The partnership signals a broader industry shift toward AI-enabled transformation in marketing, data infrastructure, and automated business processes within consumer goods, with overhauls of marketing processes to establish new measurement standards, increase conversion rates, and accelerate AI adoption across global."], [3, "Operations."], [4, "The ASM AI Fest 2026 runs through February 28th, showcasing an AI-first mindset across teaching, research, learning methods, and administration to prepare graduates and staff for pervasive AI adoption. The festival features world-class AI workshops that move beyond awareness to practical AI applications, aiming for AI to amplify human capability rather than substitute it. It concludes with a closing ceremony on February 28th, reinforcing ASM's leadership in AI-integrated education across MBA, PGDM, MCA, engineering, undergraduate studies, and school and junior college. A press release includes a photo and logo link and carries an advertorial disclaimer noting the content was provided by PR Newswire and not authored by Business Standard journalists. The initiative is described as one of the region's largest AI-driven academic efforts and positions ASM as a pioneer in AI-integrated education aligned with national AI objectives. As part of the sustained transformation, ASM will form institute-wide AI task forces, establish the ASM AI Center of Excellence, deploy the Navdrishti app for automated student lifecycle management, and introduce AI into PGDM dual specialization programs. The long-term roadmap includes institute-wise AI task forces, a center of excellence for training and research, and the Navdrishti app with AI-enabled placements and broader expansion into academics and finances. Institutional AI roadmap highlights creating task forces, a COE for training and research, and Navdrishti for automated student lifecycle management, with initial AI-enabled placements and later expansion. AI integration spans the entire ASM academic spectrum, from MBA, PGEM, MCA, and engineering to undergraduate and school junior college, preparing learners for a future with pervasive AI adoption. A PGDM dual specialization program with AI integration was launched, signaling program-level AI incorporation across curricula. Program implications include AI-driven analytics for MBA PGDM, ML tools for MCA engineering, AI-influenced entrepreneurship, and data-driven decisions for undergraduates, and foundational AI literacy for younger students. The initiative aligns with India's India AI Mission and Digital India, aiming to position India as a global hub for AI talent and to embed AI across education and administration."], [3, "Ant Group expands its open-source AI family with two trillion-parameter models, Ling-2.5-1T and Ring-2.5-1T, released under open licenses on Hugging Face and ModelScope. The move continues Ling's ecosystem expansion following Ling 2.0 unveiled in late 2025 and positions Ant Group as a key proponent of open AI distribution for researchers and developers. Ling-2.5-1T is described as a flagship general language model focused on efficient reasoning and agent interaction, capable of handling context lengths up to 1 million tokens while using about 5,890 tokens to reach frontier-like results. Ring-2.5-1T is a reasoning-optimized model with a hybrid linear architecture, delivering strong mathematical performance on IMO 2025 and CMO 2025 benchmarks. Both models are part of a coordinated Ling, Ring, and Ming strategy aimed at enterprise AI deployments that combine language understanding, reasoning, and multimodal capabilities for financial services. The open-release approach seeks to accelerate ecosystem adoption by enabling external developers to build domain-specific finance applications, potentially reducing costs and enabling larger-scale deployments. Ant Group frames these releases within a broader fintech trend of integrating large language models and reasoning systems into tasks such as compliance, customer interactions, and risk assessment. Open Access Positions: Ant Group among global contributors to open large-scale AI and supports adapting models for financial domain tasks by external developers. The Ling-2.5-1T release emphasizes efficient reasoning and agent interaction, while Ring-2.5-1T targets higher-order mathematical reasoning and benchmark performance. Overall, the announcements underscore a move toward open, collaborative AI infrastructure designed to support enterprise-grade finance use."], [0, "Cases. Tech is expanding its AI-driven frontline performance ecosystem, anchored by Realskill and Perform, to serve more than 100 enterprise clients and over 25,000 frontline agents worldwide. The goal is to improve associate proficiency and performance, including sales, across global contact centers as part of enterprise adoption. Julie Stone notes that AI alone doesn't drive performance. Translating AI insights into everyday behaviors through realistic practice and timely coaching is essential. The approach links immersive AI-powered practice, performance intelligence, and closed-loop coaching to convert AI insights into daily tasks and repeatable results, eliminating silos between learning, coaching, and execution. The ecosystem centers on RealSkill and Perform to create a continuous skills and behavior framework from onboarding through optimization, with a real-time view of frontline effectiveness. Client examples show tangible outcomes, including a 10% sales increase for an insurance firm and 17-23% NPS boosts for healthcare and telecom clients through data-informed coaching. It positions AI-enabled capabilities as industry agnostic, bridging AI investments with real business outcomes through ongoing enterprise adoption and scale. Measured outcomes include roughly 12% improvement in associate retention, 6 to 8% reductions in average handle time, 100% compliance accuracy within 60 days, a 23% rise in Net Promoter Score, and a 10% lift in sales conversion rates. TTEC highlights a global CX technology and services approach focused on AI-enabled digital CX, spanning AI, analytics, CRM, and omnichannel capabilities, with a continuous feedback loop mapping AI simulations to live coaching skills. The overall message is a cohesive AI deployment that translates automated insights into everyday frontline performance across diverse."], [3, "Industries."], [2, "This has been your Daily Brief in AI."], [1, "To read more about these stories, follow."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["News & Politics"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["artificial intelligence", "healthcare", "life sciences", "biotechnology", "education", "cloud computing", "digital transformation", "consumer goods", "marketing", "data science", "open source", "large language models", "finance", "customer service", "automation"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778148707.2159145, "duration_sec": 2.9556407928466797, "validator_hotkey": "5FZe9Mpo5dLXfhGZ4VjRnw6dmz9LVPp6nzqPyDfaS9BLKs33", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "testnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "Yeah. Yeah, man."], [1, "Well, Hickson, there's a video of him, and he did this multiple times where he would go to these gyms and he would teach a seminar, like a long seminar, and then roll with all the black belts and just tap them one after the other. One\u2014 world champions, guys that just didn't understand what was going on. Like, how is this happening? Oh yeah, like Paulo Filho when he was a WEC world champion and he was\u2014 he had won the Mundials, I believe. He'd won multiple jiu-jitsu championships. And he trained with Hickson. He's like, man, it's true. He goes, I can't believe it. He goes, that guy treated me like I didn't even belong in there. It was crazy. And Hickson by that time was probably like 40."], [0, "Yeah."], [1, "You know, and he's still just dominating guys on the mat and effortless. It wasn't strength. It was, it was just pure technique and movement."], [0, "Basics and just mastering of basics. Oh yeah."], [1, "Basics. It was like, there's none of the, no berimbolos and no X guard, nothing crazy. Everything he did is like, like jiu-jitsu 101, but to a masterful, masterful degree."], [0, "Yeah. It was incredible. And telling people that, you know, 'cause everybody knows Royce, and I'm like, you guys don't know who his big brother is."], [1, "Is Royce. He would openly say that my brother's 10 times better than me."], [0, "Right, yeah. Yeah. Yeah, so, you know, that really put, and I love jiu-jitsu because it's held up the tradition. That martial arts, so much of karate lost because it became a business. And people would just, you know, put their time in and pay for their black belts. And it just watered it down. And all these people running around saying that they're master this and, you know, grand whatever and all these made-up things. And it's like, oh yeah, the guy's a master in an Asian martial art. That's a\u2014 English word, right? You know what I mean? How did master sneak its way into it? Yeah, but anyway, but you know, male ego, you know."], [1, "Well, the thing about martial arts other than jiu-jitsu is when you're sparring, it's very controlled. Like a lot of karate sparring is very controlled. A lot of taekwondo sparring is very controlled. But in jiu-jitsu, the beautiful thing about grappling is you know how good everybody is because they all spar. They're all rolling with each other and they essentially go on full blast until the tap."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Comedy"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["brazilian jiu jitsu", "grappling", "martial arts", "technique", "fundamentals", "training", "sparring", "seminars", "black belts", "competition", "world champions", "karate", "taekwondo", "tradition"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
