ng a ten point three percent year over year gain in midsummer, the strongest increase among major United States markets."], [2, "The Property Managers Guide to Capital Expenditure Planning\nMar 24, 2026 \u00b7 Capital expenditure planning is the single most consequential financial discipline a property manager can master. Whether you oversee a commercial office block in London, a multi-family residential portfolio in Toronto, an industrial facility in Frankfurt, or a mixed-use development in Dubai, your ability to forecast, prioritize , and fund major capital expenses determines the long-term health ..."], [3, "How Much to Budget for Reserves and CapEx in Real Estate\nFeb 14, 2025 \u00b7 When you\u2019re managing real estate investments, understanding capital expenditures (CapEx) is essential for long-term asset performance and financial health. Capital Expenditures in Real Estate refer to significant investments aimed at acquiring, upgrading, or maintaining physical assets that extend beyond one year."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": null}, "prompt_chain": null, "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["boston", "office market", "commercial real estate", "real estate", "property management", "asset management", "capital expenditure", "capital budgeting", "budgeting", "financial planning", "budget forecasting", "reserve funds", "office space", "vacancy rates", "net absorption", "absorption rate", "leasing activity", "market analysis", "construction deliveries", "cash flow"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
