ge was. I mean, from the outset and from what she said, she appears to be just knowing that he had a place, not no knowing."], [0, "But that's something that's going to be very interesting and litigated here in a civil case, which is open to discoveries, open to depositions. What..."], [0, "What sort of evidence do you think they're going to be looking for? What sort of things might not, what sort of pitfalls here does Asa have to be looking out for in a civil case when people are looking for things that may look very incriminating? But look, if you're just kind of ignorant to what the hell's going on around you, may not truly be. Good question."], [0, "You know, I think one thing that's going to come up is the digital forensics. And so, you know, anyone who's been married, you often text or email with your spouse. And sometimes that's about issues or concerns or concerns."], [0, "problems that might be arising. And I'm wondering if there are any, and I don't know that there are, I'm not saying that these things exist, but there could be texts where Asa is like, hey, what were you doing last night? You said you were going to do X, but that's not true. What's going on? And then like, oh, I saw something weird downstairs. What is that? I'm just wondering if there are these little tidbits"], [0, "that could come up in a deposition about which you could be examined and say, hey, that's suspicion, isn't it? You thought something was up, didn't you? That's why you sent those messages. Now, again, I don't have any record that those such exact messages exist, but I'm wondering if during the digital forensic investigation, there might be hints and clues that also received and acted upon. And if so, does that prove knowledge or does that prove at least some modicum of knowledge? Am I?"]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["News & Politics"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "in