{"timestamp": 1778188510.9589949, "duration_sec": 2.193368434906006, "validator_hotkey": "5DkzbwTnocecNohGP4aNVcHZfUgx8uA1MGQ4WB1u3kfi78gE", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "There's a bit of a threat on Twitter. I think some of it is replacing common packages that had many dependencies with packages that, again, are primarily built to be a single dependency package. Did they just bundle it into a..."], [0, "A single package? There's been a huge push for that in the Svelte ecosystem as well, where they've been rewriting common packages to use no dependencies. So there has been a bit of a push in my ecosystem. Do exactly what you want as well. Yeah."], [0, "Lastly here, well, not lastly, there's two more things. The tag-based organization, you can now tag your stuff and filter by those tags. Just a quality of life thing. And then React Native support. Cool. I'm not using React Native, but happy these folks have React Native support inside of Storybook."], [0, "So shout out to all the teams releasing cool stuff. This is all great. I don't have nothing to complain about here. I think if the thing I complain about the most is naming of React APIs, then that's pretty good. I'm going to do that anyway. Yeah, that's great. Awesome. Yeah, tons of stuff."], [0, "Tons of new updates. We haven't really done a news show very often, but it feels like just the updates just keep on coming. It's fun to be able to talk about what's been going on. Let us know down below in the comments if you have any thoughts on any of this stuff, if you're going to be using any of it, especially the React server components. I'd love to hear your thoughts on that. Yeah. We'll catch you in the next one. Peace."]], 